"<p>When you access a fresh SaaSBase installation for the first time at <code>http://&#x3C;server-ip>:3000</code>, you will be greeted by the <strong>First-Run Wizard</strong>.</p>\n<h2>Security Safeguards</h2>\n<p>To prevent malicious actors from scanning the internet and taking over fresh installations, SaaSBase implements two primary defenses:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Setup Token Protection:</strong> If SaaSBase was installed via <code>scripts/install.sh</code>, you must enter the one-time <strong>Setup Token</strong> printed in your terminal during installation. Without this token, account creation is locked.</li>\n<li><strong>Local Host Warning:</strong> In manual or development installations without a <code>SETUP_TOKEN</code> configured, the registration page will display a prominent security notice: <em>The first person to open this page will become the instance administrator.</em></li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Option A: Registering the Administrator</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Open <code>http://&#x3C;server-ip>:3000</code> in your browser.</li>\n<li>Enter your <strong>Setup Token</strong> (if prompted).</li>\n<li>Fill in the administrator registration form:\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Admin Email:</strong> Used for security notifications and team ownership.</li>\n<li><strong>Password:</strong> Minimum 10 characters.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Complete Setup</strong>. You will be logged in immediately to the SaaSBase dashboard.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Option B: Restoring From a Backup</h2>\n<p>If you are migrating an existing SaaSBase instance to a new server:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>On the first-run screen, click <strong>Restore from a backup</strong>.</li>\n<li>Provide your <strong>Setup Token</strong>.</li>\n<li>Upload your encrypted SaaSBase self-backup file (<code>saasbase/&#x3C;date>.tar.gz.enc</code>).</li>\n<li>Enter the SHA-256 checksum and the original <code>ENCRYPTION_KEY</code> from your old server.</li>\n<li>SaaSBase will:\n<ul>\n<li>Verify file integrity against the SHA-256 hash.</li>\n<li>Decrypt and inspect the manifest.</li>\n<li>Stream and import the database dump under a non-superuser role in a single transaction.</li>\n<li>Re-encrypt credentials using the new server's key.</li>\n<li>Boot up in a <strong>Paused</strong> state to guard against split-brain scenarios.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ol>"